step 1: Install Python & pip

Check if you already have them:

python --version
pip --version


If not installed, install Python 3.9+ (recommended).

✅ Step 2: Create a Virtual Environment

Best practice is to isolate dependencies in a virtual environment.

# Create virtual environment
python -m venv venv

# Activate virtual environment
# On Linux/Mac:
source venv/bin/activate
# On Windows (PowerShell):
venv\Scripts\activate

✅ Step 3: Install Django
pip install django


Verify Django is installed:

django-admin --version

✅ Step 4: Create Django Project
django-admin startproject myproject
cd myproject


This creates a folder like:

myproject/
    manage.py
    myproject/
        __init__.py
        settings.py
        urls.py
        asgi.py
        wsgi.py

✅ Step 5: Run Development Server
python manage.py runserver


Now open your browser at 👉 http://127.0.0.1:8000/

You should see the Django welcome page 🎉

✅ Step 6: Create an App (inside project)

Django apps are modules inside the project (like users, blog, etc.).

python manage.py startapp myapp


This creates:

myapp/
    admin.py
    apps.py
    models.py
    tests.py
    views.py

✅ Step 7: Register App in Settings

Open myproject/settings.py → add your app:

INSTALLED_APPS = [
    ...,
    'myapp',
]

✅ Step 8: Create Database & Migrate
python manage.py migrate


This sets up the default SQLite database.

✅ Step 9: Create Superuser (Admin Panel)
python manage.py createsuperuser


👉 Enter username, email, password.

Run server again:

python manage.py runserver